{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\n// Method on Validator<D>.\n/// Encode the answer and atomically replace this source/criterion's record.\npub fn store_evidence<O: serde::Serialize>(\n    &self,\n    inputs: &Fingerprinted<D, O>,\n) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n```\n\nThe method saves under the source identity and criterion path captured in\n`Fingerprinted`, preserving its version, input trace, and completed answer. Encoding follows\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output`; atomic replacement follows\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage`. The result type needs\nno `Sync` bound: the method encodes the answer and captures the record and\nstorage key before constructing the storage future.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests I reviewed adequately cover `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.store_evidence`. I judged this from the supplied test sources and did not request implementation source.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n- **Key from the `Fingerprinted` identity.**\n  - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` stores records under the criterion paths `behavior`, `structure` and `text`. It then finds each stored record by its criterion path and checks the stored output.\n  - It also checks that loading afterwards returns the same source id and criterion path.\n  - `src/agent/tests.rs#fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]` stores a record under source node 1 and asserts that the record's key is node 1.\n- **Version, input trace and answer preserved.**\n  - In `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested`, the loaded record's `version()`, `dependencies()` and `output()` equal the stored value's. The tested dependencies are empty in that test.\n  - Non-empty dependencies are asserted in `tests/contracts.rs#fn[input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations]`. That test checks the stored `Dependency::Node` fingerprint.\n  - They are also asserted in `src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]`.\n  - The agent edge test checks `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` in the stored record.\n  - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records]` checks the stored version together with its dependencies.\n- **Replacing the record.**\n  - `input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations` and `tests/contracts.rs#fn[typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence]` store over an existing record. The first checks that the record now holds the new dependencies. The second checks that exactly one record remains.\n  - `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records` runs two competing stores. It asserts that one record remains and that its version, dependencies and output all come from the same save.\n- **Encoding, as required by the cited `record.output`.**\n  - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[serialization_failure_leaves_the_existing_record_unchanged]` checks that an unencodable answer returns `ValidationError::Output`. It also checks that the stored version, dependencies and output are unchanged and that no extra write happened.\n  - The encoded JSON is asserted in `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested`.\n- **Storage failure.**\n  - `src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments]` sets `fail_store`. It asserts `ValidationError::Graph(\"store\")` and that no record was written.\n  - `tests/storage.rs#fn[malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors]` covers the file-backed store path.\n- **No `Sync` bound on the result.**\n  - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync]` stores and reloads a `Cell<u32>` answer. That type is `Send` but not `Sync`.\n  - The test wraps the store call in the `send` helper. That helper presumably requires the future to be `Send`, but I did not read it.\n  - The test asserts the reloaded value is 17.\n\n**Gaps and marking**\nI found no test or marking gap and no unacknowledged gap. The remaining obligation, atomicity of the domain's replacement, belongs to the cited `evidence_storage` requirement and is not reassessed here.",
  "references": "3906913037a414bf0e63f366419c56b540e2a75f2ebcc7c0f2f06df82088f0f8",
